//==
// # Gamma- and beta-family bodies
//
// The `ProbabilityDistribution` obligations for GammaDistribution,
// BetaDistribution, ChiSquaredDistribution and StudentTDistribution. These four
// share one gap: their Mean and Variance are closed-form and implemented here,
// while every Pdf and Cdf needs the gamma or beta function (or a regularized
// incomplete form of one), none of which this tree declares. Each missing
// obligation carries a `TODO(content):` at its site rather than an
// approximation; `random.library.plato` states the gap in full.

library RandomContinuousGamma
{
    //==
    // # GammaDistribution
    //
    // Parameterization: SHAPE (k) and SCALE (theta) — theta is a scale, NOT a
    // rate; the rate form uses beta = 1 / theta. Support is x > 0.
    // Precondition: Shape > 0 and Scale > 0.
    // https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma_distribution

    // The mean: Shape * Scale.
    Mean(self: GammaDistribution): Number
        => self.Shape * self.Scale;

    // The variance: Shape * Scale^2.
    Variance(self: GammaDistribution): Number
        => self.Shape * self.Scale.Square;

    // TODO(content): Pdf(GammaDistribution, Number) is
    //   x^(k-1) * exp(-x/theta) / (Gamma(k) * theta^k)
    // which needs the gamma function. This tree declares no Gamma/LogGamma, so
    // the body is deliberately omitted rather than approximated. Implement once
    // a vetted LogGamma (e.g. Lanczos) lands in the numeric vocabulary.

    // TODO(content): Cdf(GammaDistribution, Number) is the regularized lower
    // incomplete gamma P(k, x/theta); no incomplete-gamma function exists in
    // this tree.

    //==
    // # BetaDistribution
    //
    // Parameterization: shape parameters Alpha and Beta, support the closed
    // interval [0, 1]. Precondition: Alpha > 0 and Beta > 0.
    // https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beta_distribution

    // The mean: Alpha / (Alpha + Beta).
    Mean(self: BetaDistribution): Number
        => self.Alpha / (self.Alpha + self.Beta);

    // The variance: Alpha*Beta / ((Alpha+Beta)^2 * (Alpha+Beta+1)).
    Variance(self: BetaDistribution): Number
        => self.Alpha * self.Beta
         / ((self.Alpha + self.Beta).Square * (self.Alpha + self.Beta + 1.0));

    // TODO(content): Pdf(BetaDistribution, Number) is
    //   x^(a-1) * (1-x)^(b-1) / B(a, b)
    // which needs the beta function B(a,b) = Gamma(a)Gamma(b)/Gamma(a+b); no
    // gamma or beta function exists in this tree.

    // TODO(content): Cdf(BetaDistribution, Number) is the regularized
    // incomplete beta I_x(a, b); not available here.

    //==
    // # ChiSquaredDistribution
    //
    // Parameterization: DegreesOfFreedom (k), the number of squared standard
    // normals summed. Support is x > 0. Precondition: DegreesOfFreedom > 0.
    // https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chi-squared_distribution

    // The mean: the degrees of freedom.
    Mean(self: ChiSquaredDistribution): Number
        => self.DegreesOfFreedom;

    // The variance: twice the degrees of freedom.
    Variance(self: ChiSquaredDistribution): Number
        => 2.0 * self.DegreesOfFreedom;

    // TODO(content): Pdf(ChiSquaredDistribution, Number) is
    //   x^(k/2-1) * exp(-x/2) / (2^(k/2) * Gamma(k/2))
    // which needs the gamma function; omitted for the same reason as Gamma.

    // TODO(content): Cdf(ChiSquaredDistribution, Number) is the regularized
    // lower incomplete gamma P(k/2, x/2); not available here.

    //==
    // # StudentTDistribution
    //
    // Parameterization: DegreesOfFreedom (nu), location 0 and scale 1 (this is
    // the standard, non-shifted t). Support is the whole real line.
    // Precondition: DegreesOfFreedom > 0.
    // https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Student%27s_t-distribution

    // The mean: 0 by symmetry. Precondition: DegreesOfFreedom > 1 — the mean is
    // undefined at or below one degree of freedom, where this reports 0 anyway.
    Mean(self: StudentTDistribution): Number
        => 0.0;

    // The variance: nu / (nu - 2). Precondition: DegreesOfFreedom > 2; the
    // variance is infinite on (1, 2] and undefined at or below 1.
    Variance(self: StudentTDistribution): Number
        => self.DegreesOfFreedom / (self.DegreesOfFreedom - 2.0);

    // TODO(content): Pdf(StudentTDistribution, Number) is
    //   (1 + t^2/nu)^(-(nu+1)/2) / (sqrt(nu) * B(1/2, nu/2))
    // which needs the beta function; omitted for the same reason as Beta.

    // TODO(content): Cdf(StudentTDistribution, Number) is expressed through the
    // regularized incomplete beta; not available here.
}
